1
00:00:00,076 --> 00:00:01,804
Then came 1962.

2
00:00:02,152 --> 00:00:04,804
China's army crossed into India, and India

3
00:00:04,815 --> 00:00:05,967
was caught unprepared.

4
00:00:06,315 --> 00:00:08,109
The war exposed how little the country

5
00:00:08,120 --> 00:00:10,098
knew about what lay beyond its borders.

6
00:00:11,050 --> 00:00:13,148
Kao was given the job of seeing further.

7
00:00:13,507 --> 00:00:15,311
He became the first head of the Aviation

8
00:00:15,322 --> 00:00:17,268
Research Centre at Charbatia in Odisha,

9
00:00:17,713 --> 00:00:19,648
India's new arm for aerial and technical

10
00:00:19,659 --> 00:00:20,279
intelligence.

11
00:00:21,340 --> 00:00:22,840
It was not yet an agency.

12
00:00:23,170 --> 00:00:24,877
But it was the first building block.

13
00:00:25,858 --> 00:00:28,010
After the 1965 war with Pakistan,

14
00:00:28,478 --> 00:00:30,510
Prime Minister Indira Gandhi decided India

15
00:00:30,521 --> 00:00:31,945
needed a separate service for foreign

16
00:00:31,956 --> 00:00:34,086
intelligence, answering directly to her.

17
00:00:34,434 --> 00:00:36,543
The Research and Analysis Wing was born on

18
00:00:36,554 --> 00:00:37,543
September 21,

19
00:00:38,130 --> 00:00:39,097
1968.

20
00:00:39,419 --> 00:00:41,636
It sat inside the Cabinet Secretariat.

21
00:00:41,956 --> 00:00:43,304
Kao was its first chief.

22
00:00:44,294 --> 00:00:46,577
It began with roughly 250 people and a

23
00:00:46,588 --> 00:00:48,327
budget of about two crore rupees.

24
00:00:48,696 --> 00:00:50,598
Within a few years, both had grown many

25
00:00:50,609 --> 00:00:51,327
times over.

26
00:00:51,653 --> 00:00:53,968
Kao hand-picked his officers, and demanded

27
00:00:53,979 --> 00:00:55,805
two things above all — discretion and

28
00:00:55,816 --> 00:00:56,609
professionalism.

29
00:00:57,695 --> 00:00:59,988
Inside the service, they came to be known

30
00:00:59,999 --> 00:01:00,999
as the "Kaoboys."

31
00:01:01,358 --> 00:01:02,119
According to B.

32
00:01:02,771 --> 00:01:04,651
Raman, one of the first of them, several

33
00:01:04,662 --> 00:01:06,347
would go on to lead Indian intelligence

34
00:01:06,358 --> 00:01:06,901
themselves.

